-- title:
--   An element of C[J/varpiₜ] outside every Igusa valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   The field $K$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$, and let `hK` require that $K =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, $K$ is the subfield of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the group $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with $N_0 = (q\ell)^2 M'$ and $H =$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   The base ring. Let $A$ be a henselian local discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hξA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent series equal to [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the coefficientwise image in $L$ of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1} + \dots$ of the modular invariant. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   The chart and the supersingular point. Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and `jChartFin A K j` for $j$ viewed in $C$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) such that (`hss`) for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The Drinfeld-chart hypothesis `hArig`. Let $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and $j$-inverse chart algebras along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and canonical morphism `ιFin` from $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec} C$. The hypothesis `hArig` requires: for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$ at which the germ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$, and every point $y'$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ above $z$ whose prime satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$ above, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu)$, subject to seven clauses, summarised here: (i) $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) N₀ H γ⁻¹ K τ` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; (iii) such $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ act trivially modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as in (ii) acting trivially modulo $y'$ there are an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a scalar $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ corresponding to $\tau$ under $e$ and the canonical map $C \to \mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \to \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$, $\theta$ fixing constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes of $S$ containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, and containing elements $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ and $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (v) with $a = 1$, $b = 0$, an element of $C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if all its Laurent coefficients lie in $\operatorname{algebraMap} A\,L(\mathfrak{m}_A)$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the image of the modular invariant series under `qExpand` by $q\ell$, lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for some $a_0 \in A$ with the difference in $y'$, some $e_0 \ge 1$ and some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}(\text{coeff of } X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i} \text{ in } h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit whenever $a, b \in W$ are not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, the chart image of that difference is the class of $h$.
--
--   The chosen chart at $z$. Let $z$, $\varpi z$, $y'$ be as in the hypotheses of `hArig` (with the same germ, maximality and supersingularity conditions), and assume $y'$ has prime $y$ (`hy'y`). Let $W_1$, $\sigma_1$, $f_1$, $u_1$, $v_1$ and $e_1$ be one such witness, with the isomorphism $e_1$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$, and let `hW₁` require for this witness the same seven clauses (i)–(vii) as above.
--
--   The centre $J$, the ring $B$ and the valuation ring $W$. Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$ and let `hJ` require $J$ to be the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}\bigl(\text{contraction along } e_1 \circ (\text{germ at } z) \text{ of } (\,[C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)],[X_0],[X_1]\,)\bigr)$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all $L$-algebra automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ with `IsLevelAutAt ... γ⁻¹ K τ` preserving $C$. Let $B$ be an $A$-subalgebra of $K$ and let `hB` require $B$ to be the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, regarded over $A$; thus $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and assume: `hR1`, that $C \subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; and `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and that an element of $K$ lies in $W$ exactly when it is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses there exists $b \in K$ such that $b \in B$, and such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ with the three properties: (a) an element of $L$ lies in $V$ precisely when it comes from $A$; (b) the image of $\varpi$ in $K$, whenever it lies in $V$, lies in the maximal ideal of $V$; (c) $j \in V$ and for every monic polynomial $p$ over $A$ the value $p(j)$, whenever it lies in $V$, is a unit of $V$ (not in the maximal ideal of $V$); one has $b \notin V$.
--
--   This is the Igusa-pole step in the analysis of the blow-up $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model at a supersingular point: it produces a single element of $B$ having a pole along every valuation of $K$ of Igusa type, i.e. centred on $A$, with $\varpi$ in its maximal ideal and with $j$ avoiding all monic integral relations modulo the maximal ideal. It feeds the assembly [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_mem_blowupChart_not_mem_igusaValuation_orbitPole_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_stalk_drinfeldChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_mem_blowupChart_not_mem_igusaValuation_orbitPole_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_stalk_drinfeldChart), where this clause is combined with the corresponding orbit-pole statement.
